  "title": "Jharkhand government cancels 44 exams amid protests, updates on reform and cancellations",
  "summary": "The Jharkhand government canceled 44 exams, including the JSSC-CGL examination and those conducted by the Jharkhand Public Service Commission (JPSC) and an outsourced agency, amid ongoing protests and student demands. The government has announced a reform panel and plans to address the issues.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Jharkhand government canceled 44 exams, including the JSSC-CGL examination and those conducted by the Jharkhand Public Service Commission (JPSC) and an outsourced agency.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The exams were canceled due to irregularities, with specific categories of exams listed including those for drug inspectors, deputy collectors, and forest range officers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
